{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the two angels came to Sodom in the evening.</b> Even though they arrived there without delay, as the Sages said (Berakhot 4b): Gabriel in two, Michael in one — and Scripture likewise indicated above when it says וַיֵּלְכוּ סְדֹמָה (Genesis 18:22) — nevertheless they did not enter Sodom until evening, because by then the pleas of Abraham the intercessor had already been exhausted and the judgment concluded." "<b>And he rose to meet them.</b> Lest they lodge in the square, as was then the custom in other cities when no one took in guests, and the wicked of the city harm them." "<b>And bowed his face to the ground.</b> For their appearance was fearsome without doubt."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:43.294370821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}